# Indexes, not scans or extra DBs

This repo uses Convex, not Prisma. Do not add Postgres, Prisma, raw SQL, or Directus.

## Why

- `withIndex` is type-safe and uses the schema index
- `.filter()` scans documents and will not scale to the §14 seed
- A second database duplicates the backend Convex already is

```typescript
// ❌ BAD
const user = (await ctx.db.query("users").collect()).find(
  (row) => row.email === email,
);

// ❌ BAD
await ctx.db
  .query("users")
  .filter((q) => q.eq(q.field("email"), email))
  .first();

// ✅ GOOD — schema.ts already has by_email
const user = await ctx.db
  .query("users")
  .withIndex("by_email", (q) => q.eq("email", email))
  .unique();
```

Add the index on the table in `convex/schema.ts` first (never include `_creationTime` in a custom index). If a read cannot be expressed with an index, change the schema — do not reach for SQL.
